{
  "schema": 1,
  "command": "cp",
  "help": "Usage: cp [--no-preserve=mode] [-R] [-H|-L|-P] [-f|-i|-n] [--remove-destination] [-u|--update=MODE] [-b|--backup[=CONTROL]] [-S SUFFIX] [-T] [-v] SOURCE... DEST\n{{help:help:0}}\n{{help:version:0}}\nCopying requires --no-preserve=mode. On POSIX, --remove-destination unlinks a regular file or symbolic link before copying one source. Ordinary in-place overwrite, archive and preserve modes are unsupported.\nTree validation finishes before copying; existing empty directories report no copy.\nProject alias: --dereference-command-line selects -H; GNU cp exposes only the short spelling.\nOrdinary option/operand errors exit 1; documented capability refusals retain their own status.\nOption values and operands after -- remain literal during alias normalization.\n",
